{
  "about": "The lever's predicate (kernel/src/devices.ts leverCovers): does an incident cover this browser certificate? Shared by every peer's resolver and the directory's lever so the two never disagree. Hand-written, deterministic: no keys, no signatures.",
  "rule": "covered iff (cert.kind is wdev, or dev2 via passkey) AND watt.ob === 1 AND incident.from <= cert.ceremonyAt AND (incident.to === null OR cert.ceremonyAt <= incident.to). Nothing else: not the watt.'s loggedAt (a renewal), not the directory record's enrolment loggedAt.",
  "kernel": "leverCovers(row.cert, row.watt, row.incident) === row.covered",
  "directory": "for a row with a record (the directory's wd: record for that certificate: ob, ceremonyAt, loggedAt = enrolment, renewedAt = the latest watt.), the lever over t0 = incident.from, t1 = incident.to (to null = an open window) must mark it exactly when row.covered. record null: the directory holds no wd: record for that certificate.",
